# This rig's working tree keeps the upstream reference solution out of the
# repository entirely (the verify image fetches it from the pinned commit at
# build time; gold.sh reads it from the image).
tasks/*/solution/

# Local build products (the codeaf binary run.sh copies into the container, the
# egress-proxy binaries) — untracked.
bin/

# results/ is scratch: a local working area for a run in progress. It is NOT
# durable — a task that fetches a run here loses it when the task's checkout is
# discarded, which has happened twice. fetch-results.sh therefore lands evidence
# in evidence/, which IS tracked and IS committed, so a run survives in the
# branch. Do not move evidence back under results/.
results/
!evidence/

# The run's own logs ARE evidence: egress-proxy.log is the scanner's raw input,
# and run/docker/guard logs explain a stage that failed. The repository-wide
# `*.log` ignore silently dropped them, so the first pilot's committed
# artifacts.sha256 lists an egress-proxy.log that is not in the branch — the
# scan.json is now the only record of those connections. Re-include exactly
# the run logs under evidence/, and nothing else the `*.log` rule was hiding.
!evidence/**/egress-proxy.log
!evidence/**/egress-start.log
!evidence/**/run.log
!evidence/**/docker.log
!evidence/**/guard-start.log
